<%-
# Specify admin groups by the full name of the group in the production HKey environment.
adminGroups = [
  "ondemand-admins-1025174" # HUIT OOD admin group
]
# Canvas course ID: canvas.harvard.edu/courses/170320
enabledGroups = [
  "170320" # STAT 139 - Introduction to Linear Models (Fall 2026)
]

def arrays_have_common_element(array1, array2)
  !(array1 & array2).empty?
end

userGroups = OodSupport::User.new.groups.sort_by(&:id).map(&:name)

# Three roles, all separable from the group names we already have. They decide
# who gets a personal test copy of the batch wrapper (admins only) - the class
# copy in the course folder is gated on write access instead, since that is what
# actually matters there.
#
# NOTE the staff regex needs its own pattern: canvas170320-staff-1168564 does
# NOT match /^canvas(\d+)-\d+/, because "staff" is not \d+.
userCanvasGroups = userGroups.flat_map{ |str| str.scan(/^canvas(\d+)-\d+/) }.flatten
userStaffGroups  = userGroups.flat_map{ |str| str.scan(/^canvas(\d+)-staff-\d+/) }.flatten

if arrays_have_common_element(userGroups, adminGroups)
  cluster="*"
  role="admin"
elsif arrays_have_common_element(userStaffGroups, enabledGroups)
  cluster="*"
  role="staff"
elsif arrays_have_common_element(userCanvasGroups, enabledGroups)
  cluster="*"
  role="student"
else
  cluster="disable_this_app"
  role="none"
end
-%>
---
cluster: "<%= cluster %>"
title: "RStudio - STAT 139"
description: |
  RStudio for **STAT 139** (Introduction to Linear Models), Canvas 170320.

  R comes from the course image (rocker/verse 4.5.1). Packages installed by the
  teaching staff are already on `.libPaths()`, so there is nothing to install.

  Slurm commands work in this session: `sbatch`, `squeue` and `sacct` in the
  Terminal pane, and from the R console with `system()`.

  **Running an R script as a batch job.** Copy the class script into a folder of
  your own and submit it. It runs your file in this same image with these same
  packages, so a job produces what you see here:

  ```bash
  cp ~/170320/job-tools/run-r-job.sh .
  sbatch run-r-job.sh my_script.R
  cat stat139-<jobid>.out
  ```

  You do not have to edit the script to ask for more. Options on the command
  line win over the settings in it:

  ```bash
  sbatch -c 4 -t 02:00:00 -J hw3 run-r-job.sh my_script.R
  ```

  Your job appears in `squeue -u $USER` named `stat139`, or whatever you passed
  to `-J`. Your RStudio session is the separate `sys/dashboard` row.

  **Submit from a folder you own.** The course folder is read-only to you, so a
  job started from inside it cannot write its output.

  Full instructions are in `~/170320/job-tools/README.md`. The copy in that
  folder is the class version and is always current, so copying it again gets
  you back to a working one.

  **If you would rather run the steps yourself**, the wrapper does three things:

  ```bash
  . /shared/spack/share/spack/setup-env.sh
  spack env activate apptainer
  apptainer exec -B /shared/courseSharedFolders \
    --env R_LIBS_USER=/shared/courseSharedFolders/170320outer/170320/R/x86_64-pc-linux-gnu-library/4.5 \
    /shared/apptainerImages/rstudio-base.sif Rscript my_script.R
  ```

  `R_LIBS_USER` points R at the course packages. Running through the image is
  what supplies an R that can load them: the compute node has an R of its own,
  and packages built against the container's R will not load under it.

attributes:
  imagefile: rstudio-base.sif

  # Opt in to the Slurm client injection in template/script.sh.erb, which lets
  # sbatch/squeue/sacct work from inside this app's container. Two requirements,
  # both easy to get wrong:
  #   - the value must be the string "true"
  #   - slurm_enabled MUST also appear under form: below. OOD only passes
  #     form:-listed attributes into the template context, so leaving it out
  #     makes the injection silently do nothing. A hard-coded value listed under
  #     form: is still hidden from the user in the dashboard.
  slurm_enabled: "true"

  # Course-managed R package library (created by the teaching staff)
  r_libpath: "/shared/courseSharedFolders/170320outer/170320/R/x86_64-pc-linux-gnu-library/4.5"

  # Computed above. Decides only whether this session writes a personal test
  # copy of the wrapper into $HOME (admins). MUST also appear under form: below
  # - OOD passes only form:-listed attributes into the template context, so
  # leaving it out makes the guard silently evaluate false.
  user_role: "<%= role %>"

  custom_num_cores:
    widget: "number_field"
    label: "Number of CPUs"
    value: 1
    min: 1
    max: 4
    step: 1
form:
  - custom_num_cores
  - bc_num_hours
  - imagefile
  - r_libpath
  - slurm_enabled
  - user_role
